{"html":"<p></p><figure class=\"gatsby-resp-image-figure\" style=\"\">\n    <span class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\" style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 371px; \">\n      <span class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\" style=\"padding-bottom: 100%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/jpeg;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"></span>\n  <img class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\" alt=\"save earl\" title=\"save earl\" src=\"/static/d6c5c6396566cce661f0d4ffcb29cf4a/bfbf0/saveearl.jpg\" srcset=\"/static/d6c5c6396566cce661f0d4ffcb29cf4a/db830/saveearl.jpg 256w,\n/static/d6c5c6396566cce661f0d4ffcb29cf4a/bfbf0/saveearl.jpg 371w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 371px) 100vw, 371px\" style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n    </span>\n    <figcaption class=\"gatsby-resp-image-figcaption\">save earl</figcaption>\n  </figure><p></p>\n<p>Since <a href=\"https://parade.com/97056/parade/my-name-is-earl-canceled/\" title=\"MNIE canceled\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">My Name is Earl was canceled in the EUA</a>, lots of fans started to create several petitions for the series to go on, which in my opinion is one of the funniest. If you think <a href=\"http://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/My_Name_is_Earl\" title=\"MNIE on Wikipédia\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">My Name is Earl</a> should continue, to your little quota e start following <a href=\"http://twitter.com/EarlTwitition\" title=\"EarlTwitition\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">EarlTwitition</a> profile on <a href=\"http://twitter.com/\" title=\"Official website\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Twitter</a>. It’s a fact that big companies are always looking after blogs and <a href=\"http://twitter.com/invitations/find_on_twitter\" title=\"Users on Twitter\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Twitters</a>, who knows this can work out?</p>\n<p><strong>Source:</strong> <a href=\"http://popwatch.ew.com/popwatch/2009/05/earl-fans-start.html\" title=\"My Name is Earl Twitition\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">popwatch.ew.com/</a></p>","path":"/en/blog/general/save-earl/","title":"Save Earl","language":"en","postHashId":"Z2VuZXJhbHRydWUuLi8uLi9jb3ZlcnMvMjAwOS9wb3N0LWlkLTEwMjgtY292ZXIucG5nMjAwOS0wNi0yMVQwMDowMDowMC4wMDBa","comments":[],"relatedPosts":[{"path":"/en/blog/funny/nada-by-los-pirata/","postHashId":"ZnVubnl0cnVlLi4vLi4vY292ZXJzLzIwMDgvcG9zdC1pZC0yMTItY292ZXIucG5nMjAwOC0xMS0xMVQwMDowMDowMC4wMDBa","title":"Nada by Los Pirata","date":"2008-11-11T00:00:00.000Z"},{"path":"/en/blog/funny/idol-steve-oedekerk/","postHashId":"ZnVubnl0cnVlLi4vLi4vY292ZXJzLzIwMDgvcG9zdC1pZC0xNTgtY292ZXIucG5nMjAwOC0xMC0wMlQwMDowMDowMC4wMDBa","title":"Idol: Steve Oedekerk","date":"2008-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"path":"/en/blog/general/youll-own-nothing-and-youll-be-happy-part-1/","postHashId":"Z2VuZXJhbHRydWVudWxsMjAyNi0wNS0xNlQwMDowMDowMC4wMDBa","title":"You'll own nothing and you'll be happy - Part 1","date":"2026-05-16T00:00:00.000Z"},{"path":"/en/blog/coding/website-or-app-yes-hacky-expo-router-guide/","postHashId":"Y29kaW5ndHJ1ZW51bGwyMDI2LTA0LTI1VDAwOjAwOjAwLjAwMFo=","title":"Website or App? Yes! The hacky guide to building sites with Expo Router","date":"2026-04-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"path":"/en/blog/coding/musclog-redesign-nutrition-tracking-and-why-your-fitness-app-subscription-is-a-scam/","postHashId":"Y29kaW5ndHJ1ZW51bGwyMDI2LTAzLTIyVDAwOjAwOjAwLjAwMFo=","title":"Musclog: Redesign nutrition tracking and why your fitness app subscription is a scam","date":"2026-03-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"path":"/en/blog/coding/why-the-7700-calorie-rule-is-broken-and-how-i-fixed-it-in-my-app/","postHashId":"Y29kaW5ndHJ1ZW51bGwyMDI2LTAyLTEyVDAwOjAwOjAwLjAwMFo=","title":"Why the 7700 calorie rule is broken (and how I fixed it in my app)","date":"2026-02-12T00:00:00.000Z"},{"path":"/en/blog/collectibles/why-are-som